From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 07:54:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] clk: samsung: exynos9820: Add the CMU_AUD block

The audio block of this SoC is a clock controller of its own: two PLLs,
the dividers that make the bit clocks of the four UAIF serial ports, the
codec master clock and the counter clock, and the gates of the ABOX and
of the buses around it.

Base address, mux and divider layout, gate offsets, field widths and the
parent of every gate are transcribed from the vendor clock abstraction
layer tables (drivers/soc/samsung/cal-if/exynos9820/cmucal-sfr.c and
cmucal-node.c of LineageOS/android_kernel_samsung_exynos9820 at
7d08ec364a06), by the same generator as the rest of this driver.

Both PLLs are registered as fixed rates. Their registers do read back
(CON0 to CON4; CON5 aborts), but the pll_0831x type of this driver takes
the fraction K from the register after the one holding M, P and S, while
this SoC keeps it three registers further on. The vendor table for
PLL_AUD0 holds nothing but 1179.648 MHz, trimmed by up to 840 ppb, so
the rate is a design constant; the value used is the one read back from
the running phone, M 45, P 1, S 0, K 0x5eff from 26 MHz. PLL_AUD1 is
left off by the boot loader and is registered at 0 Hz.

Every gate of the block is marked CLK_IGNORE_UNUSED for now. Nothing in
mainline holds an audio clock yet, and a gated ABOX clock makes every
access to the block hang the bus.

Signed-off-by: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/clk/samsung/clk-exynos9820.c | 472 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 472 insertions(+)

