+/*
+ * Clocks the vendor tables give a rate for but this SoC gives no readable
+ * register.  Two kinds sit here.  The on-chip oscillators have no register
+ * at all and cmucal-node.c carries them as FIXEDRATE entries.  The PLLs do
+ * have registers, but the window holding them answers no read: every attempt
+ * ends in a synchronous external abort, both from the boot loader and from
+ * here, always on the first one touched.  Registering them as PLLs is not an
+ * option either, because the core reads the register to learn the starting
+ * rate.  Their tables in cmucal-node.c hold exactly one entry each, so these
+ * are fixed by construction rather than tuned at runtime.
+ */
